    "long_instructions": "# Interactive Data App\r\n\r\n1.  **Create Interactive Filters:** Write functions to filter and sort your data. \r\n\r\n    - **Note:** Create a new list inside your function (\"copy, don't mutate\") rather than changing the original dataset.\r\n2.  **Add User Controls:** Add a \"Reset\" button to reload the original data and a label that updates dynamically (e.g., \"Showing 5 results\") whenever the list changes. Add an \"Undo\" button that removes the last filter applied.\r\n3.  **Consult AI:** Use AI to debug your logic. You might ask:\r\n      * *Why does my filtered list return zero results?*\r\n      * *How do I sort an array of objects alphabetically by a specific property?*\r\n4. **Test Your Code:** Try out the different filters and the Reset and Undo buttons. Make any revisions to your code as needed.",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Write the code for your filters, sorting, and Reset/Undo. Add active filter labels and a results count, then debug with AI to refine your logic ***(supports completing Milestone 3 tasks)***.",
